// Title: UAC Bypass Using Windows Media Player - File
// Sigma ID: 68578b43-65df-4f81-9a9b-92f32711a951
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-08-23 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1548.002
// Description: Detects the pattern of UAC Bypass using Windows Media Player osksupport.dll (UACMe 32)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/hfiref0x/UACME
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ad147b5514596e70f2782769d9833046b7c8e12b/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_uac_bypass_wmp.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath startswith "C:\\Users\\" and FolderPath endswith "\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\OskSupport.dll") or (InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\system32\\DllHost.exe" and FolderPath =~ "C:\\Program Files\\Windows Media Player\\osk.exe")
